        "value": "<p><strong><u>&nbsp;IHC Panel</u></strong><br><br><strong>IHC No-&nbsp; &nbsp; 345 /23</strong><br><strong>Gross:-&nbsp; </strong>Received paraffin tissue block No. 802/23<br><strong>Clinical Details: SQUAMOUS CELL CARCINOMA OESOPHAGUS</strong></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY RESULTS</strong></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<table class=\"Table cke_show_border\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>&nbsp;IHC Antibody</strong></td>\n<td><strong>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Immunoreactivity&nbsp; &nbsp;</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>&nbsp;CK-5/6</td>\n<td>&nbsp;STRONG POSITIVE</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>&nbsp;p63</td>\n<td>&nbsp;STRONG POSITIVE</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>&nbsp;MUC-2</td>\n<td>&nbsp;NEGATIVE</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>&nbsp;CK-7</td>\n<td>&nbsp;&nbsp;NEGATIVE</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>&nbsp;CK-20</td>\n<td>&nbsp;&nbsp;NEGATIVE</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>&nbsp;CDX2</td>\n<td>&nbsp;&nbsp;NEGATIVE</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;<br><strong>Diagnosis: Immunohistochemistry favours Squamous Cell carcinoma</strong><br><strong>Comments: Advised clinical and molecular studies correlation.</strong><br>&nbsp;<strong>Notes :</strong><br>&nbsp;1. This test was performed on the paraffin-embedded tissue section.<br>2.&nbsp;Detection system used &ndash; Biogenex &nbsp;Real Envision Detection system, peroxidase/ DAB + Rabbit/mouse.<br>3. The impression is based on the material submitted and is not a complete surgical pathology report.<br>4.&nbsp;Improper Fixation may affect results.&nbsp;<br>5. This assay has not been validated on decalified tissue. Results should be interpreted with caution given the likelihood or false negativity of decalcified specimens.</p>\n<p><br>&nbsp;<strong>Fixative requirement :</strong></p>\n<p><br>1. The volume of formalin fixative should be at least 10 times the volume of the specimen<br>2. Specimens should be immersed in 10% neutral buffered formalin within 1 hour of the biopsy/ resection procedure ( time of removal and time of immersion to be mentioned )<br>3. In all resection (large) specimens, the tumor must be bisected before immersion in fixative.</p>",
        "field": "textEditor"
      },
